D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rode</surname><given-names>CK</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayhew</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>The complete genome sequence of <italic>Escherichia coli </italic>K-12</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1997</year><volume>277</volume><fpage>1453</fpage><lpage>1474</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9278503</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Antommattei</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Weis</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Tamanoi F, Clarke S</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Reversible methylation of glutamate residues in the receptor proteins of bacterial sensory systems</article-title><source>The Enzymes</source><year>2006</year><volume>XXIV</volume><publisher-name>San Diego: Elsevier</publisher-name><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>382</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falke</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bass</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chervitz</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Danielson</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The two-component signaling pathway of bacterial chemotaxis: a molecular view of signal transduction by receptors, kinases, and adaptation enzymes</article-title><source>Annu Rev Cell Dev Biol</source><year>1997</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9442881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-